n introduces_vocab.\"}, \"counting_up\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"Start at {start}. Count up {count_by} more. What number do you land on?\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 presents counting up from a start value by a number of steps. counting up is the property the clause names.\"}, \"putting_together\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F05\", \"template\": \"One group has {a_phrase} and another group has {b_phrase}. If you put them together, how many items are there in all?\", \"reasoning\": \"F05 names putting the two groups together, which is the property the clause names.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F03\", \"F04\", \"F14\", \"F15\", \"F28\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"Add the first digits: {tens_a} + {tens_b}{v} = {tens_sum}.\", \"Add the last digits: {ones_a} + {ones_b} = {ones_sum}.\", \"{group_a_str} — There {v} {a} {name_a}.\", \"{group_b_str} — {b} more {name_b} {v} added.\", \"The dot is at {a} and it moves forward {b} {num_word}. Starting from {a}, just count up {b} {num_word}. Which number will the dot land on?\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F03 and F04 (hints) print the words 'digits' and 'digit', which the file lists in NOT_YET_KNOWN. They also print 'tens' and 'ones', also NOT_YET_KNOWN, so the hint text uses place-value vocabulary the lc may not use. F14 and F15 (question text) fill the group's noun from _EMOJI_NAMES or its plural, and the copula from _COPULAS, independently of the count slots (a for F14, b for F15). The domains derive neither from the count, so a count of 1 can print with a plural noun and a plural copula, and the noun is independent of the emoji row in group_a_str or group_b_str, which is a generator's own choice with no derivation. The printed text can then name a different object than the pictures show and give a count that does not match the number of pictures. F28 fills num_word from 'number' or 'numbers' with no derivation from b, so the same stem can print a singular n